# ===========================================================================
# FinanceAnalysis — root .gitignore
#
# Rules of the road:
#   * Keep patterns exact. A bare name such as `README.md` matches at EVERY
#     depth, so it silently untracks same-named files in subdirectories.
#   * Never re-add a bare `README.md` rule. It caused exactly that bug and was
#     removed in c931c48 ("chore(repo): un-ignore README files"). The root
#     README and nested ones (e.g. frontend/README.md) must stay tracked.
#   * `frontend/` keeps its own .gitignore (node_modules, dist, npm/vite logs);
#     those patterns are intentionally not duplicated here.
#   * Ignoring a path does NOT untrack files already committed. Anything listed
#     here is expected to be absent from the index.
# ===========================================================================


# --- Secrets & local environment configuration -----------------------------
# `.env` is an exact-name match at any depth, so it already covers
# compose/local/django/.env — a dedicated rule for that path is redundant.
# Do NOT broaden this to `.env*`: it would swallow the shared template below.
.env
!.env.example
.envs/.local


# --- Personal editor & workspace state (machine-specific) ------------------
# Multi-root workspace file: it points at a personal path outside this repo and
# carries per-user tool auto-approve rules, so it is deliberately untracked.
FinanceAnalysis.code-workspace
# Local IDE state only. .vscode/tasks.json and .vscode/git-safe.cmd remain
# tracked because they are shared with the team.
.vscode/settings.json
.vscode/git-safe.sh
.idea/
*.swp
*~


# --- OS-generated junk -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# --- Python virtual environment -------------------------------------------
.venv/


# --- Python bytecode, caches & coverage artifacts --------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc.*
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.py,cover
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pyre/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/


# --- Logs & runtime files --------------------------------------------------
# `*.log` also covers the root-level test_results.log.
*.log
*.pid
celerybeat-schedule*


# --- Local-only data & generated report packs ------------------------------
# Large, reproducible artifacts rather than project source.
reports
source_data


# --- Downloaded bootstrap installers (never project source) ----------------
get-pip.py
